title a blob carries no mode, and the tree does
prompt Open as DREAM under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first -- then pick up the running thread from the newest recommend line.
think ListAgents named no peer, so this lap carries no %291 shadow and the log says so before a file was touched. Council rota row 3 by 3548 mod 5 -- Water and Venus, care and flow. The dual seat is Growing a Language, which is this lane's own method: stand on proven ground, wear a thin costume first, diverge by strengthening. The cold roster then ran twenty-eight minutes and read 72 guards, 64 green, 8 red, tree_moved=no. Reds-first books the round, so the width boundary in glow/rune_shape.rye stayed named and untaken.
think Six of the eight trace to one habit rather than one commit: a lap that ends at the commit ships whatever a close-side --hot pass would have bitten. The exec_bit ratchet read 61 against a ceiling of 57 because the 20260827.135641 adoption landed all thirty of its files at 100644, four carrying a shebang. Rather than assert the mechanism I built a throwaway git pen and measured it: one blob 4163036efa, git show <ref>:<path> > <path> and git cat-file -p ... > both land 100644, git checkout <ref> -- <path> lands 100755. The reason is one level up from the bytes -- a blob carries no mode, the tree object does -- so any adoption that reaches for the blob loses what only the tree knew. That paragraph is now in exec-bit.md and its Cursor twin.
think The same fault then bit inside this round, which is the part worth keeping. Upstream moved mid-lap (416ae55315, another star), so the sync rota called for a rebase; git pull --rebase --autostash carried the filesystem exec bit and dropped the index one, and worktree_index_disagreements read 4. The guard's early reading exists for exactly that, and it caught it before a commit rather than months later. One git update-index --chmod=+x per file closed it.
think The nib pair is a structural finding rather than a slip. Not one of the last four nibs this card advertised resolves in this checkout -- 2efa5cf1d6, 4454c3d5d5, 1ca19833c1, a2c6180d0a. remember_git_nib_witness.rish names the cause in its own header and left it standing for Keaton's word: the seated order pins the nib then amends, so the card carries the pre-amend commit, which lives only in the authoring clone's reflog. Three stars pushing to one xy puts it beyond reach everywhere else. No word was needed to close it honestly, because that witness already accepts HEAD's parent as one of its two states, and a parent resolves in every clone. The card names 416ae55315 and takes no amend.
think Two reds are gated and they are one shape. tools/l/chatgpt-mind.sh:23 writes MAX_PROMPT_BYTES=24576, a prompt bound that merely equals living_pin_max_bytes, and that elder is pinned by SHA-256 ee508804d2 in its own compatibility receipt, so one byte breaks the MIND adaptation grant. tools/s/skate_native_core_witness.rish is reached by nothing and runs xcrun swift test, which this Linux pier has no toolchain for. Following that second one down found the thing worth surfacing: tools/fixtures/alias_sameness_scan.sh has exactly one caller, so the alias-sameness law seated 20260826.171130 has no guard that runs on this pier at all.
think A third face of %293 arrived mid-lap and was caught by the hot roster rather than by thinking. Upstream moved while this round ran, and the two commits that landed -- a5c047cefe and 416ae55315 -- left both generated pages stale: README.md's metrics block read 1,705 witnesses against a measured 1,706, and docs-geode/libraries/README.md read 5 and 1,698 where the tree holds 6 and 1,699. tools/hooks/pre-commit regenerates both and fires at git commit, yet core.hooksPath is armed per clone by tools/i/install_hooks.rish, so the wall stands only on the clones that ran it. A hook armed per clone is a promise only those clones keep. Both pages regenerated here, both witnesses GREEN, and the first hot roster was stopped rather than allowed to certify a tree the commit would not ship.
obs Measurement beat memory twice. The witness_reach evidence file on disk read 1,155 against 1,154 and was stale from an 05:03 tree; the live scan reads 1,156, and the card and the ledger carry the live number. And the mechanism behind %292 was provable in two minutes on metal rather than asserted from the shape of the diff, which is the difference between a row that teaches and a row that guesses.
obs Scope held. Seven laps of preparation on the width boundary in glow/rune_shape.rye -- 19 flagged lines, 5 fields, 5 accessors, 8 loop locals, casts falling out at 16 and 17 sites -- were measured and left for the next lap, because reds book the allocation and eight of them arrived at once.
